      "type": "legal_issue",
      "label": "Classification: Intentional vs Negligent vs Strict Liability",
      "summary": "Torts are classified by fault element: intentional (battery, false imprisonment), negligent (breach of duty of care), and strict liability (Rylands v Fletcher, certain statutory torts). Classification determines available defences and sometimes limitation periods.",
